		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=24094#p24094"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Quickstart</p><p>Create /etc/apt/sources.list.d/pgdg.list. The distributions are called codename-pgdg. In the example, replace wheezy with the actual distribution you are using:</p><p>deb <a href="http://apt.postgresql.org/pub/repos/apt/" rel="nofollow">http://apt.postgresql.org/pub/repos/apt/</a> wheezy-pgdg main<br />---------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br />deb : commande introuvable , n&#039;est pas supporté par ubuntu<br />---------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p><p>Le postgres que j&#039;ai effacé communiquait mal avec postgis<br />Je veux éviter des installations mal embarquées</p>]]></content>
